# NestedText v3 — DOMAIN-TYPE-DEFINITION table for dtd-creation-suite-rot-domain
# Read by the skill, never quoted as argumentation (LAW.SUITE.1).
#
# TWO LAYERS. The top layer is INTENT: what a user wants, in their words.
# The layer beneath is FAMILY: which of the seventeen families that intent
# reaches. A family is never an intent and an intent is never a family.
#
# shape, intent row:    intent > needs > variants > families > commands > gate > example
# shape, unmatched row: unmatched > routes-to > gate > proof
#
# A reader that finds a field the shape does not declare reports the surplus
# and reads the declared ones (LAW.REC.4); the two shapes are distinct and an
# intent row is never read with the unmatched shape.
#
# UNMATCHED IS PROVABLY EMPTY: every one of the seventeen families declared in
# checker/readme-index.mjs is named under at least one intent below. The proof
# is the families layer itself, and a family absent from it is a finding.

screenshot-hosting:
    needs: screenshots recognized, hosted inside the document, model recreates visuals
    variants: SVG, XHTML, SCHEMATIC, CHAIN
    families: The Graphic and Geometric Suite, Prompt creators one per schematic
    commands: codebase-surveyor-dtd, codebase-generator-dtd, typography-dtd, brainstorm-meta-clear-section-dtd
    gate: ask where hosted, chain for survey then generate
    example: i need to create a new skill but i want screenshots recognized and hosted inside that very document

research-asking:
    needs: understand how, one-time ask, save-my-cache bridge
    variants: RNG, ENT, MOD, DITA, CHAIN, SKILL
    families: Research, Asking and deciding
    commands: deep-dive-dtd, hadal-deep-dive-dtd, hadopelagia-deep-dive-dtd, ask-me-questions-dtd, ask-me-everything-dtd
    gate: ask where deep, cache bridge where long
    example: i need to understand how example triggers research then deep-dive with ask where allowed

single-then-next:
    needs: one command only, followed by no-ask commands, suggest what runs next
    variants: CHAIN, FRAMEWORK
    families: The Phantom Books shelf, Thinking models
    commands: any single command, then chain-dtd suggestion
    gate: none on the first, ask on the suggestion
    example: phantom or pareto run alone, skill suggests the measured next

cache-drift-timeout:
    needs: save-ur-cache mid-work, work-in-progress redirect, drift patches directives debugging
    variants: NVDL, XSL, CHAIN
    families: Asking and deciding, Tasks
    commands: ask-me-many-questions-dtd, chain-dtd, task-handoff-dtd
    gate: save-ur-cache bridge, drift activation beside running work
    example: direction change in-between via timeout law, drift drafted not interrupted

skill-creation:
    needs: new skill with routing, schematics, forms, proof
    variants: SCHEMATIC, SKILL, DCL, XSD
    families: Creators, Prompt creators one per schematic, File types and dorks
    commands: create-agent-skill-dtd, create-prompt-nt-dtd, create-filetype-nt-dtd, brainstorm-meta-clear-section-dtd
    gate: creators gate always (LAW.ASK.10)
    example: create a skill through twelve questions that are never skipped

many-lenses:
    needs: one problem seen from genuinely different angles, never averaged into consensus
    variants: FRAMEWORK, CHAIN, SCHEMATIC
    families: The RoT MoE lenses, Thinking models
    commands: rot-elevate-dtd, rot-chroma-dtd, first-principles-dtd, inversion-dtd, second-order-dtd
    gate: none on a single lens, ask before a chain of them
    example: i am too close to this decision, show me what i am not seeing

repo-and-growth:
    needs: measure this repository's face, or grow the codebase by a declared verb
    variants: DITA, DITAMAP, RELS, CHAIN
    families: Repository, Codebase growth
    commands: git-gh-amplification-dtd, git-gh-matrix-scala-dtd, amplify-codebase-dtd, enhance-codebase-dtd, overhaul-codebase-dtd
    gate: ask the band before any verb above amplify
    example: build me a gate.yml that tests this on three operating systems

judge-my-artifact:
    needs: is this skill, command, subagent or prose actually any good
    variants: SCH, XSPEC, FRAMEWORK
    families: Audits in the foreground
    commands: audit-skill-dtd, audit-slash-command-dtd, audit-subagent-dtd, ai-slop-dtd
    gate: none, these scan the whole context instead of asking
    example: read this skill i wrote and tell me what is wrong with it

argument-plumbing:
    needs: how commands pass things to each other, what the dollar tokens mean, how to chain them
    variants: ENT, MOD, DCL, CHAIN
    families: The sigil, Inter-operation
    commands: sigil-dtd, verbs-dtd, chain-dtd
    gate: none on explanation, ask before emitting a chain
    example: i do not understand what the sigil section is for

policy-and-lists:
    needs: forbid this, allow that, star the good ones, and hold the rule afterwards
    variants: SOC, SCH, NVDL
    families: The lists
    commands: file-blacklist-dtd, code-blacklist-dtd, file-graylist-dtd, code-graylist-dtd, file-whitelist-dtd, code-whitelist-dtd, starlist-dtd, starlist-manager-dtd
    gate: gray list asks its declared question (LAW.CORE.8)
    example: never let this dependency into the tree again

work-in-flight:
    needs: what runs next, what is still open, heal what broke, debug what fails
    variants: DITAMAP, CHAIN, FRAMEWORK
    families: Workflow and the Adiutor
    commands: whats-next-dtd, add-to-todos-dtd, check-todos-dtd, run-plan-dtd, heal-skill-dtd, debug-dtd, RoT-DtD-Commander-Adiutor
    gate: none, these read the run in progress
    example: what should i do next in this repository

unmatched:
    routes-to: ask-me-questions-dtd
    gate: standard
    proof: all seventeen families of checker/readme-index.mjs are named above; unmatched is reached only by an intent no family claims, and a family missing from the layer above is a finding of kind domain
